.TH heliosctl-streams 1 0.3.0 "heliosctl 0.3.0" "Helios Manual"
.SH NAME
heliosctl\-streams \- A device\*(Aqs streams: list, get, start, stop, update, set\-destination
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl streams\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
A device\*(Aqs streams: list, get, start, stop, update, set\-destination
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-list(1)
A device\*(Aqs streams: desired and reported state
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-get(1)
One stream
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-start(1)
Start a stream (desired state live)
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-stop(1)
Stop a stream (desired state stopped)
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-update(1)
Change a stream\*(Aqs source, profile, bitrate, source ceiling or recording
.TP
heliosctl\-streams\-set\-destination(1)
Set where a stream goes: an srt:// or srtla:// URL
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBheliosctl\fR(1), for exit status, environment, files and security.
